    sum of squares(column-loading) = 1

    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
        Variable |    Comp1     Comp2     Comp3     Comp4     Comp5     Comp6 
    -------------+------------------------------------------------------------
    Support_Ge~1 |   0.4512   -0.1272    0.0690   -0.6420   -0.3429    0.4957 
    Support_Ge~2 |   0.4765   -0.2723    0.1088   -0.1833   -0.0708   -0.8052 
    Support_Ge~3 |   0.4223   -0.1617    0.5108    0.2456    0.6370    0.2616 
    Support_Ge~4 |   0.2448    0.8945    0.3195    0.0311   -0.1592   -0.1076 
    Support_Ge~5 |   0.3826    0.2526   -0.7623   -0.0879    0.4479    0.0186 
    Support_Ge~6 |   0.4298   -0.1400   -0.1984    0.6965   -0.4956    0.1598 
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------

.         
.         * Generate controls
.         // Gender of the respondent
.         rename sex Gender

.         // Age of the respondent
.         g Age=syear-gebjahr

.         // Marital Status of the respondent
.         g Marital_Status=pgfamstd if pgfamstd>0
(88 missing values generated)

.         // Employment status
.         rename pgemplst Employment_Status

.         // Income (Net)
.         g Income_Net=pglabnet if pglabnet>=0
(8,423 missing values generated)

.         replace Income_Net=0 if pglabnet<0 & Employment_Status==5 // Income_N
> et is assumed to be zero for individuals who are not employed and who did not
>  declaire any income (pglabnet=-2)
(8,423 real changes made)

.         // Education in years
.         g Education_In_Years=pgbilzeit if pgbilzeit>=0
(225 missing values generated)

.         // Number of Children up to the observation year
.         g Num_Sons=0

.         forvalues i=1(1)19{
  2.                 qui replace Num_Sons=Num_Sons+1 if kidsex`i'==1
  3.                 }       

.         g Num_Children=Num_Daughters+Num_Sons

.         // Migraation background
.         rename migback Migration_Background

.         // Sample region
.         g Sample_Region=sampreg if sampreg>0
(1 missing value generated)

.         // Religion
.         g Religion=plh0258_h if plh0258_h>0
(14,890 missing values generated)

.         // Parents minimum education level      
.         g Parents_Min_Edu=min(msedu, fsedu) if fsedu>=0 & msedu>=0
(2,990 missing values generated)

.         // Current health
.         g Current_Health=ple0008 if ple0008>0
(29 missing values generated)

. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 *
.         * Verbal description of the model: Support_Gender_Equality = β₀ + β₁ 
> * Having_Daughters + Controls + ε 
.         
.         * We consider a: linear OLS regression
. 
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis (with robust s
> tandard errors) using pc1_Support_Gender_Equality as dependent variable and t
> he dummy variable Having_Daughters as independent variable. 
.         reg pc1_Support_Gender_Equality Having_Daughters Gender Age Marital_S
> tatus Employment_Status Income_Net Education_In_Years Num_Children Migration_
> Background Sample_Region Religion Parents_Min_Edu Current_Health, vce(robust)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =        786
                                                F(13, 772)        =       6.09
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0000
                                                R-squared         =     0.0914
                                                Root MSE          =     1.6276

